.el .ds Aq '
.TH devin-plugins-remove 1  "remove " 
.SH NAME
devin\-plugins\-remove \- Remove an installed plugin (auto\-installed requireds are left in place)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBdevin plugins remove\fR [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-\-local\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fINAME\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Remove an installed plugin (auto\-installed requireds are left in place)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Remove even if another installed plugin or a governance config still requires it. A governance\-required plugin is reinstalled on the next session in the requiring scope
.TP
\fB\-\-local\fR
Remove from this machine only. Fails for plugins that are in your personal plugins
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip the interactive cloud\-removal confirmation
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fINAME\fR>
The installed plugin name (or a disambiguated `owner/repo` label when several installed plugins share the same name)
